\section{Structural Validation: Concrete \& Composite Material Integrity}
\label{sec:structural-validation}

\subsection{Overview}
To ensure that the physical hardware containers, cryogenic anchor pads,
and high-pressure containment vessels supporting the Uranus
Unprecedented Simulation (UUAS) can withstand extreme mechanical,
thermal, and vibrational loads, a comprehensive structural validation
suite was executed. All tests were performed under conditions
representative of high-pressure planetary simulation environments.

\subsection{Testing Scope}
The validation suite evaluates:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Ultra-high compressive strength performance.
    \item Cryogenic thermal shock resistance.
    \item Dynamic vibration damping under magnetic shielding.
    \item Hydrostatic boundary sealing under mantle-analog pressures.
\end{itemize}

