\subsection{Results}
All structural materials exceeded required thresholds:
\begin{itemize}
    \item UHPFRC demonstrated elite compressive strength suitable for
    high-pressure containment frames.
    \item Cryogenic silica-dense concrete maintained full structural
    integrity under rapid thermal cycling.
    \item Barite-concrete achieved high damping performance for vibration
    isolation and magnetic shielding.
    \item High-pressure grout exhibited near-impermeable sealing
    characteristics under mantle-analog pressures.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Conclusion}
The structural validation suite confirms that all concrete and composite
materials engineered for UUAS hardware infrastructure exceed the
mechanical, thermal, vibrational, and permeability requirements for
extreme planetary simulation environments. These results establish the
structural reliability of the UUAS physical architecture and ensure safe
operation under high-pressure and cryogenic conditions.